#X obj 640 11 rhythm.hexbeat;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 292 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Generates a rhythmic pattern from a hexadecimal value.
Each hex digit is expanded into four bits (a nibble) \, and the resulting
bit sequence is output as a list of 1s and 0s. For example \, the value
#D1 expands to 1101 0001 \, which can be fed directly into a sequencer
\, a step display \, or a trigger source.;
#X text 240 184 Typical use cases: quickly entering 4- or 8-step drum
patterns using compact hex notation (#D1 instead of 1 1 0 1 0 0 0 1)
\, building longer patterns by concatenating several hex values (for
example \, #A4C8 gives 12 steps) \, or generating variations of patterns
programmatically by manipulating hex strings.;
#X text 240 285 When a list of hex values is sent to the inlet \, the
object outputs a sequence of patterns \, one for each argument — this
is convenient for displaying a whole row at once in [ui.matrix] or
a similar display.;
